{"h":3390,"w":2400,"lines":[{"h":0.033430233395556841,"y":0.0058139530575510578,"x":0.0082135492068117818,"c":1,"t":"@MirsIELTS","w":0.30390144348144532},{"t":"Introduction","x":0.071868587190926495,"y":0.04651162811448506,"h":0.013081394746943475,"c":1,"w":0.11704311370849609},{"t":"Writing","y":0.091967386292535203,"w":0.084118690490722667,"h":0.019139393944304195,"x":0.073015503110487809,"c":1},{"h":0.016021815162141073,"y":0.11769911494995455,"x":0.073921965152533742,"t":"This test consists of two tasks. It is suggested that candidates spend about 20 minutes on","w":0.81108830769856777,"c":1},{"x":0.073861602517454231,"t":"Task 1, which requires them to write at least 150 words, and 40 minutes on Task 2, which","y":0.13453856486831617,"w":0.80505996704101568,"h":0.019392190218675109,"c":1},{"h":0.014749262536873142,"x":0.071868584036589786,"y":0.1539823008039245,"t":"requires them to write at least 250 words. Task 2 contributes twice as much as Task 1 to the","w":0.82956878662109379,"c":1},{"h":0.015245887733842056,"y":0.1726081163122869,"t":"Writing score.","x":0.07352253312943631,"w":0.13006918589274091,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.79671457926432299,"y":0.18895348848660509,"t":"Task 1 requires candidates to look at a diagram or some data (in a graph, table or chart)","h":0.016061260707258884,"x":0.094455851969815111},{"y":0.20639534875511645,"t":"and to present the information in their own words. They are assessed on their ability to","w":0.78028747558593747,"x":0.073921967802513866,"h":0.016023530087991511,"c":1},{"t":"organise, present and possibly compare data, and are required to describe the stages of a","c":1,"x":0.073921977995827601,"y":0.22529069778999022,"w":0.81519505818684912,"h":0.01600723716713337},{"w":0.63871932983398427,"y":0.24213732335358007,"h":0.018246227028095641,"c":1,"t":"process, describe an object or event, or explain how something works.","x":0.073851764007658333},{"y":0.26001108399226047,"h":0.019242937656278825,"t":"In Task 2, candidates are presented with a point of view, argument or problem. They are","c":1,"x":0.094408533079449727,"w":0.79476776123046866},{"y":0.27758112085160214,"t":"assessed on their ability to present a solution to the problem, present and justify an opinion,","h":0.01747701864326956,"c":1,"w":0.8295687866210939,"x":0.073921972570617431},{"c":1,"w":0.81724848429361974,"h":0.017493311564127589,"y":0.29646017677907932,"x":0.073921958992468534,"t":"compare and contrast evidence and opinions, and evaluate and challenge ideas, evidence"},{"h":0.014749262536873142,"t":"or arguments.","y":0.31533923326228608,"c":1,"x":0.073921976405554826,"w":0.13141682942708333},{"h":0.019469033300349214,"c":1,"y":0.33059696055487209,"t":"Candidates are also assessed on their ability to write in an appropriate style. More","w":0.743461201985677,"x":0.096447592577063881},{"h":0.018413486311921079,"x":0.073881725264687836,"t":"information on assessing the Writing test, including Writing assessment criteria (public","c":1,"w":0.77832372029622399,"y":0.3487760017390058},{"c":1,"h":0.017518179114237697,"t":"version), is available at ielts.org.","x":0.073921967731235105,"y":0.36773255814924954,"w":0.29568789164225262},{"t":"Speaking","w":0.10537137349446614,"h":0.019509581619307714,"c":1,"x":0.075651068952769338,"y":0.39722195327840149},{"t":"This test takes between 11 and 14 minutes and is conducted by a trained examiner.","y":0.42296511601505749,"w":0.75359344482421875,"h":0.013081395872223012,"x":0.078028739515381265,"c":1},{"y":0.44186046531746781,"w":0.20123203277587889,"t":"There are three parts:","h":0.014534883302221635,"x":0.075975359269029402,"c":1},{"w":0.057494869232177712,"h":0.013274336283185861,"x":0.075975357892847165,"c":1,"t":"Part 1","y":0.47079646017893562},{"y":0.49126010505512485,"c":1,"h":0.017369715372721251,"t":"The candidate and the examiner introduce themselves. Candidates then answer general","w":0.79886398315429685,"x":0.075932481700857771},{"t":"questions about themselves, their home\/family, their job\/studies, their interests and a wide","y":0.510029498390563,"w":0.81108830769856777,"c":1,"h":0.017699115044247815,"x":0.075975353297455778},{"h":0.016041537934699868,"c":1,"t":"range of similar familiar topic areas. This part lasts between four and five minutes.","x":0.073921982140081471,"y":0.52761627918209109,"w":0.74332646687825521},{"h":0.013108835248468953,"c":1,"w":0.059548257191975901,"y":0.55811209465978273,"t":"Part 2","x":0.075975357957986822},{"x":0.075975353708112717,"y":0.57846607646943216,"w":0.80287475585937507,"h":0.016010667581473847,"c":1,"t":"The candidate is given a task card with prompts and is asked to talk on a particular topic."},{"h":0.014573471947053829,"c":1,"y":0.59734513249280097,"w":0.77618067423502601,"t":"The candidate has one minute to prepare and they can make some notes if they wish,","x":0.078028759287953831},{"c":1,"w":0.78028747558593747,"h":0.014749262536873142,"t":"before speaking for between one and two minutes. The examiner then asks one or two","y":0.61474926233828164,"x":0.078028746689190409},{"c":1,"y":0.6321533924576449,"t":"questions on the same topic.","x":0.075975364049357119,"w":0.26488705952962238,"h":0.016224188790560423},{"h":0.015056199943069837,"t":"Part 3","x":0.075850398011861248,"y":0.66253003925694431,"c":1,"w":0.059798177083333348},{"x":0.078028754166845141,"w":0.8151950581868489,"c":1,"y":0.68459302299239067,"t":"The examiner and the candidate engage in a discussion of more abstract issues which are","h":0.013081395872223012},{"x":0.073921972355208157,"y":0.70203488383648982,"t":"thematically linked to the topic in Part 2. The discussion lasts between four and five minutes.","w":0.8377823384602866,"h":0.015988371857499573,"c":1},{"t":"The Speaking test assesses whether candidates can communicate effectively in English.","c":1,"w":0.80492813110351558,"x":0.09650924030520637,"y":0.71946902657263945,"h":0.015996089586466145},{"x":0.075975367165516727,"w":0.83983571370442722,"h":0.017487308761011455,"c":1,"t":"The assessment takes into account Fluency and Coherence, Lexical Resource, Grammatical","y":0.73687315632071282},{"h":0.017525039380278939,"w":0.82546198527018233,"y":0.75427728600052857,"c":1,"x":0.075975379479898394,"t":"Range and Accuracy, and Pronunciation. More information on assessing the Speaking test,"},{"x":0.073921962279403036,"t":"including Speaking assessment criteria (public version), is available at ielts.org.","w":0.72073923746744784,"y":0.77315634208818373,"h":0.01754133230113708,"c":1}]}